    Measure 2: voice 2's quarter rest on the upper staff, with voice 5's A3 (stem down) crossing up into the upper staff.
      Voice 1 has no note on beat 1 (forward).
    Before the fix, both rests left their staff towards the other staff: voice 5 is an upper voice, so its rest was put
    above the cross-staff note and its stem, between the staves, and voice 2's rest below the cross-staff note, between the staves.
    The cross-staff notes belong to the other staff's voices, so the rests stay in their staves now.
    Measure 3: voice 1's quarter rest above voice 5's B4 (stem up) crossing up into the upper staff.
    Measure 4: voice 6's quarter rest below voice 1's G3 (stem up) crossing down into the lower staff.
      Voice 5 has no note on beat 1 (forward).
    In measures 3 and 4, the rests still avoid the cross-staff notes: they move away from the other staff.
